From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 18:11:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] usb: hub: give root hubs the same power-on-good floor

hub_power_on_good_delay() applies a 100ms minimum to every hub EXCEPT root
hubs, which get bPwrOn2PwrGood*2 unfloored.  On Sky1 that value is ~0, so
hub_activate()'s INIT2/INIT3 sampling runs roughly 20/40ms after port power.

A downstream hub behind that root port cannot re-attach that fast.  If it has
not attached by the time INIT3 samples, the connect is never observed: the
port is left at PLS=Polling with CCS=1 -- the device IS electrically present
and the port IS powered -- but PED=0 and the hub driver is never told to reset
it, so dmesg shows no port errors at all.

Measured on O6N, installer, stick in a USB-A port behind a VIA Labs VL812:

  portsc = 0x0c0006e1  Speed=1 Link=Polling CCS PP WDE WOE
  /proc/partitions: no sd* at all
  /sys/bus/usb/devices: root hubs only, zero downstream devices

Unbinding and rebinding the hub driver -- which re-runs hub_activate() at a
calmer moment -- enumerates the entire tree immediately: the VL812, a mouse, a
keyboard, and the medium as sda with three partitions.

The same kernel enumerates fine on the INSTALLED system, where boot is slower
and userspace re-triggers, which is consistent with this being a timing race
rather than a missing driver or a PM problem.

Give root hubs the same floor as everyone else.  Worst case this costs ~100ms
of boot on a port that was ready anyway.

Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/usb/core/hub.h
+++ b/drivers/usb/core/hub.h
@@ -166,10 +166,20 @@
 {
 	unsigned delay = hub->descriptor->bPwrOn2PwrGood * 2;
 
-	if (!hub->hdev->parent)	/* root hub */
-		return delay;
-	else /* Wait at least 100 msec for power to become stable */
-		return max(delay, 100U);
+	/*
+	 * Root hubs used to get bPwrOn2PwrGood*2 with no floor, which on Sky1
+	 * is ~0, so INIT2/INIT3 run ~20/40ms after port power.  A downstream
+	 * hub behind that root port needs longer than that to re-attach, and
+	 * if it has not by the time INIT3 samples the port the connect is
+	 * simply never seen: the port stays PLS=Polling with CCS=1 and the hub
+	 * driver is never told to reset it.  Measured on O6N, where a VL812
+	 * carries the installation medium and nothing enumerated until the hub
+	 * driver was unbound and rebound by hand.
+	 *
+	 * Give root hubs the same 100ms floor as every other hub.  Cost is at
+	 * most ~100ms of boot on a port that would have been ready anyway.
+	 */
+	return max(delay, 100U);
 }
 
 static inline int hub_port_debounce_be_connected(struct usb_hub *hub,
